# How to cite mosaic. GitHub's "Cite this repository" and Zenodo read this file; mosaic's
# Help > Cite mosaic reads its copy in mosaic/data/CITATION.cff (the two are kept the same, and
# each release sets their version and date).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mosaic in your work, please cite it as below."
title: mosaic
abstract: >-
  A desktop app for assembling multi-panel scientific figures. Plots placed as PDF or SVG go into
  the exported PDF or SVG unchanged and stay linked to their files; pages take journals' figure
  sizes; and a check before export compares text sizes, line widths and picture resolution with
  the journal's rules.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Davis
    given-names: Matthew
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8933-349X"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthewwdavis/mosaic"
url: "https://github.com/matthewwdavis/mosaic"
keywords:
  - scientific figures
  - multi-panel figures
  - figure assembly
  - journal figure requirements
